steps.do:
From the get_accounts result, check that all of these hold:
(1) at least one personal checking account (account_type checking) with status OPEN;
(2) the new account will not take the customer above 6 business checking accounts;
(3) no account has status CLOSED;
(4) an OPEN personal checking account has a balance of at least $500.
If (1) fails: explain that an OPEN personal checking account is needed first. If the customer asks, run the personal checking opening procedure, then re-run get_accounts.
If (2) or (3) fails: tell the customer which requirement is not met, do not open the account, and stop.
If only (4) fails: offer fund_checking. If the customer declines, explain that the balance must reach $500 first, and stop.
